# Positive: the world actually has the shapes this script exercised —
# a character, at least one location, and an item that changed hands.
type: character
type: location
type: item

# Negative: the engine's own referential-integrity checks on the <state>
# block — a dangling `location`, an id reused, a reference to nothing —
# never fired. This is the state-consistency check: it is already run by
# worldstate.go on every block, so the smoke test just has to watch for it.
!\[state: .*could not be created
!\[state: .*was skipped
!\[state: .*was left alone
!\[state: .*refers to something that does not exist
!\[state: .*is not a usable id
!\[state: .*is gone; ids are never reused
!\[uncorrected:
